Well, I don't realy understand why people make it so difficult: training
their pets. I find this a time consuming method. I use my pet in an
entirely different manner. I polymorph him into something big (e.g. a
gray draggon or a jabberwock or something like that). Then I simply walk
into the shop, stand back and watch him kill the shopkeeper. Since I did
not kill him myself, I think this does not affect my luck, or allignment.
Then I can pick up any item i want, all the shopkeepers gold and usually
a skeleton key.

There is a problem with big pets however. They tend to kill anything you
come across (also co-alligned priests and unicorns) so sometimes you have
to make sure they stay away from things you don't want killed.

Kris.

PS: if you have cloak of magic resistance (standard wizard equipment) a
great way to polymorph your pet is to make him walk over a polymorph trap
until he turns into something you like. Only problem is when he turns
into a jelly and won't move of the trap. That's where the cloak comes in:
You can safely move onto the trap and push him of and back on, because
the trap won't affect you.


